course: dictionary
lesson: 2883
title: Finding meaning from place clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A doorstep is the step, or flat spot, just outside a front door. Context helps you check this. «She waits on the doorstep in her coat for two hours.» She is in her coat and waiting, so she is outside, not inside the warm house.
explain: The word can also mean very close to where you live. When a phrase says «on your doorstep», read the other words to see if it means a place outside the door or something very near. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
explain: Sentences can show feelings too. «Maddie sat on her doorstep holding a tissue to her mouth» tells you where she is and hints that she is upset. Clues like the tissue help you understand the whole story.
fact: A doorstep is the step or flat spot just outside the front door of a house.
fact: «On your doorstep» means very close to where you live.
fact: Parcels, milk and post are often left on the doorstep.
fact: «Right on our doorstep» means very near.
fact: Context clues, like «waits» or «sat», tell you where the doorstep is.
exercise: «She waits on the doorstep in her coat for two hours.» Where is she waiting? | At the top of the stairs | *Outside the front door | Inside the kitchen | In the garden shed
exercise: «A police officer stood on Kieran's doorstep asking about a bike.» What does doorstep mean here? | A shop on the high street | A bell that rings when people visit | *The step just outside the front door | A door made of wood
exercise: Dad says the new library is «right on our doorstep». What does he mean? | It is only open on Sundays | *It is very close to where we live | It is far away across the country | It is a shop that sells doors
test: «Maddie sat on her doorstep holding a tissue to her mouth.» Where was Maddie sitting? | On a bus | *Outside her front door | In a school hall | Under the bed
test: What does «on your doorstep» mean? | Inside your bedroom | Far from home on a trip | *Very close to where you live | A type of door lock
exam: Ella says a doorstep is a door. Why is she wrong? | She is right | *A doorstep is the step outside the door, not the door itself | A doorstep is a kind of door | Doorsteps are always inside the house
